install-patch-proposal.diff - a PROPOSAL for bearstonem/d2r-pcvr, for you to read and change as you like.
It is NOT applied and your tests were NOT run: it was written against the files of origin/main at a0a4f5f
(v0.3.19), as they read in git, and only checked to apply without fuzz to copies of those files (patch --fuzz=0 -p1),
for the patched Python and PowerShell to parse, and for the patched Inno script to compile with a dummy payload.

Part 1: the launcher's descriptor of your mod, written with the mod
  vrmod-manifest.json                  new file at the repo root (beside d2r_pcvr.ini)
  steamvr/install.py                   puts it into mods\D2R-PCVR\ like the plugin and modinfo.json (payload; journaled, so a
                                       restore / removal takes it away; nothing is written outside your own mod folder)
  steamvr/package.py                   adds it to the release ZIP's file list
  installer/stage_native_installer.py  adds it to the installer's allowlist (ROOT_FILES)
  steamvr/mod_identity_test.py         a test that its version, id and names agree with the release (and that both lists carry it)
  steamvr/install_test.py              two lines: it is there after install, gone after restore
  docs/RELEASING.md                    step 2 of the release checklist names the manifest's version beside the other version places

Part 2: the D2R VR Launcher inside your installer (optional, nothing changes without the two new build parameters)
  installer/build_native_installer.ps1 -LauncherSetup <D2R_VR_Launcher_Setup_x.y.z.exe> -LauncherSetupSha256 <pin>: checks name and pin,
                                       hands the file to the staging script, passes three defines to the Inno compiler, records it in .build.json
  installer/stage_native_installer.py  stages that one file, unmodified, as launcher\<name> in the payload (exact name, pinned hash,
                                       listed in the payload's release-manifest.json so /PAYLOADCHECK covers it)
  installer/stage_native_installer_test.py   wrong pin, wrong name and the good case
  installer/D2R_PCVR_Setup.iss         only when the defines are given: at the start of the post-install step, if HKCU\Software\D2R VR
                                       Launcher shows no launcher (or no program) or an older one, and the file still has the pinned hash,
                                       run it silently as the original user, log the exit code and ignore it. Your wizard is untouched.
  installer/README.md                  a paragraph on it
Per release: the "version" in vrmod-manifest.json (the new test fails when it lags behind), and the launcher pin when you take a newer launcher.
Apply with:  git apply install-patch-proposal.diff     (or: patch -p1 < install-patch-proposal.diff)

